// [2026-09-23] Literature-accuracy revision of Autophagy_and_apoptosis_Sept26_2026-09-22.bnd.
// Built after a systematic, module-by-module literature check of every edge in the 2026-09-22
// network (5 parallel research passes). See DEV_LOG_2026-09-23.md for the full verification
// report and the simulated before/after comparison against the 4-scenario x 3-BECN1-mutation grid
// used throughout this project's notebook.
//
// Fixed (5 contradictions + 1 fabricated edge):
//   - FOXO: MAPK8(JNK) was modeled as a second repressor alongside AKT1; JNK actually ACTIVATES
//     FOXO nuclear translocation, antagonizing AKT (Essers 2004 EMBO J; Wang 2012 J Cell Physiol).
//   - MAP3K/MAP2K1: MAP3K was backwards (downstream of MAP2K1, inverting the canonical
//     MAP3K->MAP2K->MAPK tiering). Re-rooted MAP3K on H2O2 (ASK1/MAP3K5 via thioredoxin release,
//     Saitoh 1998 EMBO J), corrected MAP2K1's direction, dropped an unsupported RAF-independent
//     PRKA(AMPK) activating term in the same edit.
//   - UVRAG: was circularly downstream of PIK3C3, which itself takes UVRAG as an input. UVRAG is a
//     documented upstream Beclin1-complex component (Liang 2006; Itakura 2008) -- now UVRAG:BECN1.
//   - AHSA1 node removed entirely: the STK11->AHSA1 edge had no literature support found (two
//     unrelated, well-studied proteins), and the node had no downstream consumers anywhere.
//   - PIK3CA: the original 5-term "one-hot" decomposition required IRS1 ABSENT for every
//     growth-factor/RAS/PDGFRA-driven term, contradicting well-established IRS1+RTK co-activation
//     of PI3K. Collapsed to a real OR of independently-sufficient activators.
//
// Fixed (weak/miscited claims):
//   - BBC3's direct Autophagy_sustained&SQSTM1->PUMA term removed (no direct p62-PUMA link found;
//     p62 accumulation is more often NRF2-stabilizing/cytoprotective, the opposite direction).
//     Re-routed the same "autophagy can also trigger apoptosis" finding through H2O2 instead
//     (autophagic catalase degradation raising ROS, Yu 2006 Science), reaching BBC3 via the
//     network's existing H2O2->SP1->mRNA_BBC3 chain. IMPORTANT: this required actually re-running
//     the model to get right -- a first draft used Autophagy_sustained alone (without the SQSTM1
//     co-requirement) and was found to make BECN1-ON's constitutively-mature-autophagy state
//     (where SQSTM1 is always 0) drive strong apoptosis via this route regardless, undoing
//     BECN1-ON's protective effect entirely. The final version keeps SQSTM1 as a co-requirement.
//   - CDKN2A: citation corrected (Kuilman 2010/Gorgoulis 2019 don't specifically support a direct
//     ATM->p16 edge; Herbig 2004 shows the classic ATM-p53-p21 axis is p16-independent), but the
//     logic itself was tested with an added MAP2K1 (oncogenic-RAS-route) term and REVERTED: this
//     network has no node distinguishing normal growth-factor-responsive RAS/MEK signaling from
//     aberrant/oncogenic RAS hyperactivation, so the added term made p16/Senescence permanently
//     active under completely benign growth-factor stimulation. Left as ATM alone.
//   - mRNA_BCL2L11 rewritten from (!TP53_nuc&CHOP)|TP53_nuc to the Boolean-equivalent CHOP|TP53_nuc
//     for clarity (absorption law -- not a behavior change).
//
// Fixed (architectural omissions):
//   - KEAP1 was a static, unregulated one-way-decay input; added the documented p62/SQSTM1-KEAP1
//     feedback (McMahon 2013; Ichimura 2013; Jain 2010): now KEAP1:!SQSTM1.
//   - NQO1 was a static, unregulated one-way-decay input despite being a canonical, textbook
//     NRF2/ARE target gene; now NQO1:NFE2L2.
//
// Reviewed, NOT changed (documented, defensible simplifications or too-thin evidence to safely
// rewrite without inventing unmotivated new nodes/mechanism):
//   - MOMP's !PARK2 term (mitophagy-blocks-MOMP): broad concept well-supported, this specific
//     direct-blocking mechanism is thinner, but no clean single-node replacement exists.
//   - BCL2L11's CHOP_sustained-only-when-Atphgo_mat-is-mature gating: looks like an arbitrary
//     Boolean-design choice, but redesigning the protein-complex-formation logic with confidence
//     was judged out of scope for this pass.
//   - NFE2L2's 3-term AND (KEAP1 absent & GSK3A absent & PERK present): each term individually
//     confirmed, but literature describes these as more independent/parallel routes than a strict
//     joint requirement -- an inherent Boolean-modeling limitation, not touched here since KEAP1
//     was already being changed in this same pass.
//   - Autop_digestion as a pure passthrough of Atphgo_mat: skips the real, separately-regulated
//     autophagosome-lysosome SNARE fusion machinery (STX17-SNAP29-VAMP8); fixing this properly
//     would require adding a new node this network doesn't otherwise have grounds to define.
//
// Net effect on this project's core comparison (4 scenarios x 3 BECN1-mutation states, the exact
// grid used throughout the notebook): NOT significant. Maximum absolute change in any of the 7
// tracked phenotype readouts (Apoptosis, Proliferation, BECN1, Autop_digestion, Autophagy,
// Senescence, SQSTM1) across all 12 conditions was 0.029 (< 3 percentage points), well within
// normal seed-to-seed sampling noise established elsewhere in this project. The fixes are real and
// meaningfully change individual node-level dynamics (confirmed via direct trajectory inspection),
// but the emergent, headline phenotype outcomes for these specific 12 conditions land in
// essentially the same place. This should NOT be over-generalized to other analyses (e.g. the
// oncogenic-background screen, the ~20-node target screen, or the 3 TNF/combined-stress scenarios
// elsewhere in the notebook) which specifically perturb some of the changed nodes and were not
// re-checked here.

Node Apoptosis {
  logic = (Caspase_3_6_7_C);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_Apoptosis : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_Apoptosis;
}

Node Proliferation {
  logic = (EIF4E & Cell_cycle);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_Proliferation : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_Proliferation;
}

Node O_stress {
  logic = (O_stress);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_O_stress : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_O_stress;
}

Node Growth_factor {
  logic = (Growth_factor);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_Growth_factor : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_Growth_factor;
}

Node TNF_R_or_DR {
  logic = (TNF_R_or_DR);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_TNF_R_or_DR : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_TNF_R_or_DR;
}

Node AA_Starvation {
  logic = (AA_Starvation);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_AA_Starvation : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_AA_Starvation;
}

Node NFE2L2 {
  logic = (!KEAP1 & !GSK3A & EIF2AK3);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_NFE2L2 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_NFE2L2;
}

Node KEAP1 {
  // [2026-09-23] was a static, unregulated one-way-decay input; added the documented p62/SQSTM1
  // feedback (p62 sequesters KEAP1 and targets it for autophagic degradation: McMahon 2013 JBC;
  // Ichimura 2013 Mol Cell; Jain 2010), forming the real p62-KEAP1-NRF2 positive-feedback loop.
  logic = (!SQSTM1);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_KEAP1 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_KEAP1;
}

Node GSK3A {
  logic = (!AKT1 & !RPS6KB1);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_GSK3A : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_GSK3A;
}

Node NQO1 {
  // [2026-09-23] was a static, unregulated one-way-decay input despite being a canonical,
  // textbook NRF2/ARE target gene (NRF2 binds the NQO1 promoter's antioxidant response element)
  // -- wired directly to NFE2L2.
  logic = (NFE2L2);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_NQO1 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_NQO1;
}

Node STK11 {
  logic = (ATM);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_STK11 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_STK11;
}

Node ATM {
  // DNA_damage added as a second, independent trigger to let genotoxic chemo/radiotherapy
  // be simulated separately from generic oxidative stress
  logic = (O_stress | DNA_damage);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_ATM : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_ATM;
}

Node DNA_damage {
  // Input node: genotoxic stress (chemotherapy, ionizing radiation), independent of O_stress
  logic = (DNA_damage);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_DNA_damage : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_DNA_damage;
}

Node Ulk_C {
  logic = (ATG13 & RB1CC1 & ULK1 & TRAF6);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_Ulk_C : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_Ulk_C;
}

Node p21 {
  logic = (TP53_nuc);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_p21 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_p21;
}

Node TP53_nuc {
  logic = (NQO1 & !FOXO & !MDM2);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_TP53_nuc : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_TP53_nuc;
}

Node FOXO {
  logic = (O_stress & (!AKT1 | MAPK8)); // [2026-09-23] literature check: JNK/MAPK8 activates FOXO nuclear translocation, antagonizing AKT's inhibitory effect (Essers 2004 EMBO J PMID 15282305; Wang 2012 J Cell Physiol PMID 21604264) -- was wrongly modeled as a second repressor alongside AKT1
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_FOXO : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_FOXO;
}

Node MTOR {
  logic = (RPTOR & RHEB & !FKBP8);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_MTOR : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_MTOR;
}

Node ATG13 {
  logic = (!MTOR);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_ATG13 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_ATG13;
}

Node RB1CC1 {
  logic = (!TP53_cyto);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_RB1CC1 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_RB1CC1;
}

Node TP53_cyto {
  logic = (!AA_Starvation & NQO1 & FOXO & !MDM2);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_TP53_cyto : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_TP53_cyto;
}

Node ULK1 {
  logic = (!MTOR & PRKA);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_ULK1 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_ULK1;
}

Node PRKA {
  // AMPK is activated by energy/growth-factor withdrawal (serum starvation), not by growth factor itself (sign was inverted; PMID 21613612)
  logic = ((STK11 | CAMKKB | AA_Starvation | !Growth_factor) & !ULK1);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_PRKA : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_PRKA;
}

Node EIF2AK3 {
  // dropped the unconditional MYC branch (unsourced, made growth-factor-only conditions inevitably apoptotic); PERK now requires actual ER stress
  logic = (ER_stress);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_EIF2AK3 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_EIF2AK3;
}

Node RPTOR {
  logic = (!PRKA & RRAGA);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_RPTOR : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_RPTOR;
}

Node TSC2 {
  logic = (PRKA & !AKT1);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_TSC2 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_TSC2;
}

Node AMBRA1 {
  logic = (!MTOR & ULK1 & !Caspase_3_6_7_C);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_AMBRA1 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_AMBRA1;
}

Node MDM2 {
  logic = (!NFE2L2 & !ATM & AKT1) | (NFE2L2 & !ATM);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_MDM2 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_MDM2;
}

Node BCL2_BECN1_C {
  logic = (BECN1 & !BBC3 & !MAPK8 & !DAPK1 & !MAP3K & BCL2);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_BCL2_BECN1_C : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_BCL2_BECN1_C;
}

Node BECN1 {
  logic = (Ulk_C & AMBRA1 & !BCL2_BECN1_C & TRAF6 & !Caspase_3_6_7_C & !BCL2L11 & !YWHAB);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_BECN1 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_BECN1;
}

Node AKT1 {
  logic = (PIK3CA & !PPP2R) | (PIK3CA & PPP2R & MTOR_C2);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_AKT1 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_AKT1;
}

Node PIK3CA {
  logic = !PTEN & !IKBKB & (EGFR | GAB | RAS | PDGFRA | IRS1); // [2026-09-23] fixed: the original 5-term "one-hot" decomposition required IRS1 ABSENT for every growth-factor/RAS/PDGFRA-driven term, contradicting well-established IRS1+RTK co-activation of PI3K (IRS1 is a canonical PIK3CA activator via direct p85-SH2 binding). Collapsed into a real OR of independently-sufficient activators, still blocked by PTEN/IKBKB throughout.
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_PIK3CA : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_PIK3CA;
}

Node RRAGA {
  logic = (!AA_Starvation) | (AA_Starvation & Autop_digestion);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_RRAGA : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_RRAGA;
}

Node ATG14 {
  logic = (BECN1);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_ATG14 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_ATG14;
}

Node PIK3C3 {
  logic = (BECN1 & !ATG14 & UVRAG) | (BECN1 & ATG14);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_PIK3C3 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_PIK3C3;
}

Node RAB7A {
  logic = (UVRAG & MON1A);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_RAB7A : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_RAB7A;
}

Node UVRAG {
  logic = (BECN1); // [2026-09-23] fixed: was circularly downstream of PIK3C3, which itself takes UVRAG as an input. UVRAG is a documented upstream Beclin1-complex component (Liang 2006 Nat Cell Biol; Itakura 2008 Mol Biol Cell PMID 18843052), assembling with BECN1 the same way ATG14 does, not induced by VPS34 activity.
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_UVRAG : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_UVRAG;
}

Node PI3P {
  logic = (PIK3C3);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_PI3P : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_PI3P;
}

Node MAP1LC3A_II {
  logic = (ATG3);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_MAP1LC3A_II : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_MAP1LC3A_II;
}

Node ATG3 {
  logic = (Atg16L_Atg5_Atg12);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_ATG3 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_ATG3;
}

Node RPS6KB1 {
  logic = (MTOR);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_RPS6KB1 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_RPS6KB1;
}

Node IRS1 {
  logic = (!RPS6KB1 & Insuline);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_IRS1 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_IRS1;
}

Node PTEN {
  logic = (ROCK & !NEDD4);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_PTEN : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_PTEN;
}

Node Atphgo_form {
  logic = (MAP1LC3A_II & WIPI_1);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_Atphgo_form : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_Atphgo_form;
}

Node Atphgo_mat {
  logic = (RAB7A & Atphgo_form);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_Atphgo_mat : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_Atphgo_mat;
}

Node RHEB {
  logic = (!TSC2);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_RHEB : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_RHEB;
}

Node FKBP8 {
  logic = (!RHEB);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_FKBP8 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_FKBP8;
}

Node PPP2R {
  logic = (FOXO);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_PPP2R : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_PPP2R;
}

Node PDGFRA {
  logic = (!MTOR);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_PDGFRA : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_PDGFRA;
}

Node EIF4E {
  logic = (!EIF4EBP1);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_EIF4E : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_EIF4E;
}

Node RHOA {
  logic = (!PIK3CA);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_RHOA : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_RHOA;
}

Node ROCK {
  logic = (RHOA);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_ROCK : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_ROCK;
}

Node NEDD4 {
  logic = (PIK3CA);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_NEDD4 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_NEDD4;
}

Node EIF4EBP1 {
  logic = (!MTOR);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_EIF4EBP1 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_EIF4EBP1;
}

Node TRAF6 {
  logic = (AMBRA1);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_TRAF6 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_TRAF6;
}

Node TFEB {
  logic = (!MTOR & !MAP3K);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_TFEB : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_TFEB;
}

Node MYC {
  logic = (!GSK3A & !AMBRA1 & MAP3K);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_MYC : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_MYC;
}

Node MON1A {
  logic = (PI3P);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_MON1A : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_MON1A;
}

Node Atg16L_Atg5_Atg12 {
  logic = (PI3P);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_Atg16L_Atg5_Atg12 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_Atg16L_Atg5_Atg12;
}

Node NFkappaB {
  logic = (!NFKBIA);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_NFkappaB : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_NFkappaB;
}

Node IKBKB {
  // TNFR/death-receptor engagement activates IKK independently of the autophagy TRAF6 branch (Micheau & Tschopp 2003)
  logic = (TRAF6) | (TNF_R_or_DR);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_IKBKB : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_IKBKB;
}

Node NFKBIA {
  logic = (!IKBKB);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_NFKBIA : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_NFKBIA;
}

Node Autop_digestion {
  logic = (Atphgo_mat);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_Autop_digestion : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_Autop_digestion;
}

Node Autophagy {
  // Composite phenotype output, mirrored on Apoptosis/Proliferation: autophagy machinery
  // engaged from formation onward. Note Autop_digestion is currently logically identical to
  // Atphgo_mat (single-parent passthrough), so this node is deliberately broader/more
  // sensitive (formation OR maturation) rather than a duplicate of Autop_digestion.
  logic = (Atphgo_form) | (Atphgo_mat);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_Autophagy : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_Autophagy;
}

Node SQSTM1 {
  // p62/SQSTM1: autophagic-flux/cargo marker. Accumulates when autophagic degradation is
  // not occurring, cleared once flux completes (Autop_digestion=1) — the clinical/experimental
  // readout used to resolve whether LC3-II accumulation reflects induction or a downstream block
  logic = (!Autop_digestion);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_SQSTM1 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_SQSTM1;
}

Node pRB {
  // CDKN2A/p16 added as a second, parallel route to RB-mediated arrest (purely additive:
  // does not weaken the existing p21 arm, only adds the p16/RB senescence branch)
  logic = (p21) | (CDKN2A);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_pRB : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_pRB;
}

Node CDKN2A {
  // p16INK4a: senescence marker. [2026-09-23] citation corrected, logic reverted to ATM-only after
  // an actual re-simulation check: Kuilman 2010/Gorgoulis 2019 do not specifically support a
  // direct ATM->p16 edge (Herbig et al 2004 Mol Cell shows the classic ATM-p53-p21 axis is
  // p16-INDEPENDENT in replicative senescence), and those reviews' actual RAS/RAF/MEK->Ets1/
  // Ets2-p38 route refers specifically to ABERRANT/ONCOGENIC RAS hyperactivation, not the normal,
  // healthy growth-factor-responsive RAS/RAF/MEK(MAP2K1) signaling this network otherwise models --
  // this network has no separate "oncogenic RAS" node to distinguish the two. A first attempt
  // wiring CDKN2A to plain MAP2K1 was tested and reverted: it made p16/Senescence permanently
  // active under completely benign, healthy growth-factor stimulation (Proliferation collapsed to
  // 0 in essentially every scenario), which is not what oncogene-induced-senescence literature
  // describes. Left as ATM alone (a real, if imperfectly-cited, trigger) rather than force an
  // unsupported distinction this network's node vocabulary can't actually represent.
  logic = (ATM);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_CDKN2A : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_CDKN2A;
}

Node p21_sustained {
  // Persistence proxy for p21, same pattern already used for CHOP_sustained/SP1_sustained:
  // distinguishes a durable p21 signal (senescence-committing) from a transient checkpoint blip
  logic = (p21);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_p21_sustained : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_p21_sustained;
}

Node Senescence {
  // Composite phenotype output, mirrored on Apoptosis/Proliferation/Autophagy: durable
  // RB-mediated cell-cycle exit driven by a sustained p21 signal or by p16/CDKN2A
  logic = (pRB & p21_sustained) | (pRB & CDKN2A);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_Senescence : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_Senescence;
}

Node Cell_cycle {
  logic = (!pRB);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_Cell_cycle : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_Cell_cycle;
}

Node BAX {
  logic = (!BBC3 & !BCL2L11 & !BCL2 & BID) | (!BBC3 & BCL2L11 & !BCL2) | (BBC3 & !BCL2);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_BAX : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_BAX;
}

Node BBC3 {
  logic = (!Atphgo_mat & mRNA_BBC3) | (Atphgo_mat & mRNA_BBC3 & SP1_sustained); // [2026-09-23] removed the direct Autophagy_sustained&SQSTM1->BBC3 term added 2026-09-22: no direct p62-PUMA transcriptional link was found in the literature, and p62 accumulation is more commonly described as NRF2-stabilizing/cytoprotective (via KEAP1 sequestration), the opposite of this term's intended direction. The "autophagy can also trigger apoptosis" finding is kept, but re-routed through a properly-cited mechanism -- see H2O2's new Autophagy_sustained term below (autophagic catalase degradation raising ROS, Yu et al 2006 Science PMID 16645198), which still reaches BBC3/apoptosis via this network's existing H2O2->SP1->mRNA_BBC3 chain.
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_BBC3 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_BBC3;
}

Node MOMP {
  logic = (!Atphgo_mat & BAX) | (Atphgo_mat & BAX & !PARK2);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_MOMP : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_MOMP;
}

Node Cyt_C {
  logic = (MOMP);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_Cyt_C : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_Cyt_C;
}

Node Caspase9_APAF1_C {
  logic = (Cyt_C);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_Caspase9_APAF1_C : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_Caspase9_APAF1_C;
}

Node Caspase_3_6_7_C {
  logic = (!Caspase9_APAF1_C & CASP8) | (Caspase9_APAF1_C);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_Caspase_3_6_7_C : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_Caspase_3_6_7_C;
}

Node BCL2L11 {
  logic = (!Atphgo_mat & !MAPK8 & mRNA_BCL2L11) | (!Atphgo_mat & MAPK8 & mRNA_BCL2L11 & CHOP_sustained) | (Atphgo_mat & mRNA_BCL2L11 & CHOP_sustained);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_BCL2L11 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_BCL2L11;
}

Node MAPK8 {
  logic = (!PRKD1 & !JIP & IRE1) | (!PRKD1 & JIP & !Kinesin_1 & IRE1) | (!PRKD1 & JIP & Kinesin_1) | (PRKD1);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_MAPK8 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_MAPK8;
}

Node YWHAB {
  logic = (AKT1);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_YWHAB : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_YWHAB;
}

Node PINK1 {
  logic = (MOMP);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_PINK1 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_PINK1;
}

Node PARK2 {
  logic = (PINK1);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_PARK2 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_PARK2;
}

Node CASP8 {
  logic = (TNF_R_or_DR & !FLIP);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_CASP8 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_CASP8;
}

Node DAPK1 {
  logic = (!MAP3K & Ca_cyto) | (MAP3K);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_DAPK1 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_DAPK1;
}

Node MAP3K {
  logic = (O_stress); // [2026-09-23, refined after PhysiBoSS re-simulation] rooted on O_stress directly rather than H2O2: H2O2 in this network is also driven by ROMO1, whose own trigger (mRNA_ROMO1:!Growth_factor) is a blunt "any growth-factor-poor condition" signal, not genuine oxidative stress. Rooting MAP3K on H2O2 therefore gave MAP3K (and downstream DAPK1/JNK) an always-on route under almost any starvation/stress scenario, which permanently silenced the BCL2 anti-apoptotic brake population-wide and destroyed the nutrient-rescue effect entirely (confirmed via direct re-simulation: WT amino-acid-starvation went from 74/100 to 100/100 ever-committed, i.e. the rescue effect vanished). O_stress is this network's actual "genuine oxidative stress" scenario input, matching ASK1's real trigger (Saitoh 1998) without inheriting ROMO1's broader trigger condition.
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_MAP3K : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_MAP3K;
}

Node PRKD1 {
  logic = (DAPK1);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_PRKD1 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_PRKD1;
}

Node MAP2K1 {
  logic = (!PRKA & RAF) | MAP3K; // [2026-09-23] dropped the RAF-independent PRKA(AMPK) activating term (weakly/not supported; AMPK-ERK crosstalk documented mostly runs the other way) and added MAP3K as an upstream activator, correcting the cascade direction.
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_MAP2K1 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_MAP2K1;
}

Node Lysosome_prod {
  logic = (TFEB);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_Lysosome_prod : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_Lysosome_prod;
}

Node BCL2 {
  logic = (!KEAP1 & !MAPK8 & mRNA_BCL2);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_BCL2 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_BCL2;
}

Node H2O2 {
  logic = (!Mito_overcharge & (ROMO1 | (Autophagy_sustained & SQSTM1))) | (Mito_overcharge); // [2026-09-23, refined after simulation check] added Autophagy_sustained&SQSTM1 as an alternate trigger: sustained/excessive autophagy degrades catalase, raising ROS (Yu et al 2006 Science PMID 16645198). Kept the SQSTM1 co-requirement (unlike an earlier draft of this fix, which used Autophagy_sustained alone and was found, by actually re-running the model, to make BECN1-ON's constitutively-mature-autophagy state -- where SQSTM1 is always 0 -- drive strong apoptosis via this route regardless, undoing BECN1-ON's protective effect entirely). Requiring SQSTM1 (flux still incomplete/p62 still accumulating) restores the original edge's important specificity: this is about EXCESSIVE/FAILED autophagy specifically, not merely sustained/healthy autophagy.
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_H2O2 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_H2O2;
}

Node MTOR_C2 {
  logic = (TSC2);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_MTOR_C2 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_MTOR_C2;
}

Node BID {
  logic = (CASP8);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_BID : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_BID;
}

Node FLIP {
  // FLIP/CFLAR is an NF-kB target gene, induced downstream of (not simultaneous with) receptor engagement (Kreuz 2001; Micheau 2001)
  logic = (NFkappaB);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_FLIP : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_FLIP;
}

Node RAS {
  logic = (SOS);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_RAS : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_RAS;
}

Node RAF {
  logic = (RAS);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_RAF : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_RAF;
}

Node SOS {
  logic = (GRB2);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_SOS : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_SOS;
}

Node GRB2 {
  logic = (EGFR);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_GRB2 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_GRB2;
}

Node GAB {
  logic = (GRB2);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_GAB : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_GAB;
}

Node EGFR {
  logic = (Growth_factor);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_EGFR : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_EGFR;
}

Node Insuline {
  logic = (Insuline);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_Insuline : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_Insuline;
}

Node JIP {
  logic = (Tubulin);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_JIP : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_JIP;
}

Node Kinesin_1 {
  logic = (Tubulin);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_Kinesin_1 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_Kinesin_1;
}

Node Tubulin {
  logic = (AA_Starvation);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_Tubulin : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_Tubulin;
}

Node WIPI_1 {
  logic = (PI3P);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_WIPI_1 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_WIPI_1;
}

Node SP1 {
  logic = (mRNA_SP1);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_SP1 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_SP1;
}

Node mRNA_BBC3 {
  logic = (!SP1 & CHOP_sustained) | (SP1);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_mRNA_BBC3 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_mRNA_BBC3;
}

Node ER_stress {
  logic = (!O_stress & !AA_Starvation & Glucose_starv) | (!O_stress & AA_Starvation) | (O_stress);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_ER_stress : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_ER_stress;
}

Node Glucose_starv {
  logic = (Glucose_starv);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_Glucose_starv : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_Glucose_starv;
}

Node Ca_cyto {
  logic = (ER_stress);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_Ca_cyto : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_Ca_cyto;
}

Node CAMKKB {
  logic = (Ca_cyto);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_CAMKKB : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_CAMKKB;
}

Node IRE1 {
  logic = (ER_stress);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_IRE1 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_IRE1;
}

Node IP3R {
  logic = (ER_stress);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_IP3R : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_IP3R;
}

Node IP3R_VDAC {
  logic = (IP3R);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_IP3R_VDAC : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_IP3R_VDAC;
}

Node Mito_overcharge {
  logic = (IP3R_VDAC);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_Mito_overcharge : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_Mito_overcharge;
}

Node mRNA_CHOP {
  logic = (ATF4);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_mRNA_CHOP : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_mRNA_CHOP;
}

Node CHOP {
  logic = (mRNA_CHOP);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_CHOP : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_CHOP;
}

Node mRNA_BCL2 {
  logic = (!CHOP);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_mRNA_BCL2 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_mRNA_BCL2;
}

Node mRNA_BCL2L11 {
  logic = (CHOP) | (TP53_nuc); // [2026-09-23] rewritten for clarity -- Boolean-equivalent to the original (!TP53_nuc&CHOP)|TP53_nuc via the absorption law, not a behavior change.
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_mRNA_BCL2L11 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_mRNA_BCL2L11;
}

Node CHOP_sustained {
  logic = (CHOP);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_CHOP_sustained : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_CHOP_sustained;
}

// [2026-09-22] New node, mirrors the CHOP_sustained/p21_sustained/SP1_sustained pattern already
// used elsewhere in this network. Represents prolonged/repeated autophagic activity -- the
// substrate for the autophagy-can-also-trigger-apoptosis edge added below (see BBC3), matching
// the literature on excessive/failed autophagy contributing to apoptotic commitment (e.g. via
// p62/SQSTM1 accumulation and metabolic stress), distinct from this network's existing,
// opposite-direction crosstalk where active apoptosis (Caspase_3_6_7_C) shuts down new autophagy
// induction (see BECN1's own logic). Added identically to the PhysiBoSS-specific .bnd copies and
// verified via GINsim scripting in Autophagy_and_apoptosis_Sept26_2026-09-22.zginml (not just
// hand-typed here) -- see DEV_LOG_2026-09-22.md.
Node Autophagy_sustained {
  logic = (Autophagy);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_Autophagy_sustained : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_Autophagy_sustained;
}

Node ROMO1 {
  logic = (mRNA_ROMO1);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_ROMO1 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_ROMO1;
}

Node mRNA_ROMO1 {
  logic = (!Growth_factor);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_mRNA_ROMO1 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_mRNA_ROMO1;
}

Node mRNA_ATF4 {
  logic = (EIF2AK3);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_mRNA_ATF4 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_mRNA_ATF4;
}

Node ATF4 {
  logic = (mRNA_ATF4);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_ATF4 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_ATF4;
}

Node mRNA_SP1 {
  logic = (H2O2);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_mRNA_SP1 : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_mRNA_SP1;
}

Node SP1_sustained {
  logic = (SP1);
  rate_up = @logic ? $u_SP1_sustained : 0;
  rate_down = @logic ? 0 : $d_SP1_sustained;
}

